{
	title: 'Protect queued messages while editing',
	spec: 'Terminal and web support editing human queued messages without dequeueing them during the edit. Up on an empty composer selects the newest queued human message; web waiting queued rows also offer Edit. Identify the editor as Editing queued message, never a delivered-prompt edit. The host atomically protects the inbox identity before exposing authoritative text and pauses the session; if delivery wins the race, visibly reject rather than pretending it is queued. Enter or Save replaces the message in the same queue position; Alt-Enter while editing also saves, never creates a duplicate. Escape, Cancel, Down with unchanged text, or saving empty text cancels without changing the message. Preserve the pre-existing draft, original queue timestamp and unsaved edit text across disconnect, reload and navigation. On save or cancel resume only if starting this edit caused the pause; an explicit later pause or close suppresses resume. Continue cannot bypass a queue edit from either client or command; delivered-prompt editing retains its distinct continue behavior. Acquisition and saves validate connection ownership, message identity and command IDs. Disconnect releases the connection hold and leaves a visible durable pause; reconnect reacquires before saving, and client loss never leaves a permanent unexplained hold or loses typed text. Failed reacquisition preserves changed text as draft recovery and reports the full failure. Safe reads and drafts remain available during editing; destructive queue and conversation operations cannot bypass the hold. Queue edits save literal message text, not slash-command execution. Queue links are not required. A durable sessions/<id>/queue-edit.ason pause intent is enforced before takeover recovery, even if the old host flushed partial output or a tool was still settling; legitimate turn starts clear it. Reconnect must compare authoritative text with the originally acquired text and recover rather than silently overwrite another edit. Replay of an already-saved submit releases only a matching reacquired hold without repeating the edit. Open questions visibly refuse queue editing.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'User raised the race explicitly: a queue message must not be dequeued while it is being edited. Current amend.begin recalls the latest human inbox item without pausing; this is insufficient. Proposed, not yet agreed: newest queued message first, and resume on save/cancel only when beginning the edit caused the pause. Delivered-prompt edits remain distinct. Host acquisition must precede opening the editor; a client-local pause or disabled button is not a concurrency guarantee.',
		'User authorized implementation with the proposed defaults: newest human queued message first, and resume only when acquisition paused an active session. Holds are connection-owned, installed synchronously before pause/text reply, and snapshots broadcast only the held inbox identity, never an ownership token. Both clients share queue-edit state beside the ordinary draft; cancellation retains changed text for re-edit, and lost/conflicting acquisition recovers it into the draft. Queue saves use the existing deduplicated submit path and preserve inbox identity, order and receipt timestamp.',
		'An early artificial turn_end is not enough for takeover safety: shutdown can flush an assistant block after it, or interrupted tools can settle later. Durable pause intent uses validated liveFiles state, enforced by both host.ready paths before recovery. Natural running-turn completion remains intact. Every legitimate turns.start clears the intent, including explicit queue-next and clear continuations; held sessions cannot start. Delayed automatic resume waits for settlement and respects subsequent pause, close or disconnect. Direct model slash commands also check the hold.',
